  /* ---------------- the words: the arcade, together ----------------

     Hangman, Scrabble, chess, Pictionary and Spymaster — the games that need
     a room. Nearly every line here has somebody's name in it, and names change
     places between languages ("{name}’s move" is 「{name}の番」, «Ход: {name}»,
     "{name} की चाल"), so none of them is glued together in English order.

     **Nobody's gender is guessed.** A name could belong to anyone, so the
     Russian avoids past-tense verbs after one («Победа за {name}» rather than
     «{name} выиграл»), the Hindi and Urdu say whose win it was rather than who
     won ("{name} की जीत"), and "you" is the polite plural wherever a language
     marks it. The chess terms are the ones chess players use: 詰み (checkmate
     in Japanese chess writing), 将死, мат, शह-मात, شہ مات, كش مات. */

